Package: homelab-cli
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3-requests, python3-yaml, python3-argcomplete
Recommends: bash-completion
Description: Command-line client for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Register/login/whoami/logout against homelab-api's JSON REST API, look
 up a feature's address in the service registry, and (nearly all the
 same activities as the web UIs) read/send email via direct IMAP/SMTP
 (XOAUTH2, using the same saved JWT -- no separate mail login), manage
 files via homelab-drive's Bearer-token JSON API, and (site_admin
 accounts only) manage users/roles via homelab-api's admin endpoints.
 Session (token/refresh_token) is stored 0600 in
 ~/.config/homelab-cli/session.yml, separate from the non-secret
 api_base/drive_base/imap_*/smtp_* config. The one shipped package in
 this ecosystem deliberately allowed to be Python rather than Perl (see
 CLAUDE.md's Language section) -- a good fit for a pure CLI tool that's
 mostly argument parsing and HTTP/IMAP/SMTP calls, and easy for a Linux
 user to read, edit, or take apart for their own purposes.
